// ---- java.util containers: element-level, so writes and reads compose ----
// A read is `Argument(0).\[] -> Return` and a write is `... -> Argument(0).\[]`, the two
// halves of one prefix substitution. Mixing a bare read with an element-level write (or the
// reverse) silently composes to nothing: the write would put taint one level below where the
// read looks for it.
// Writers carry BOTH `Argument(1)` and `Argument(2)` because these methods are overloaded on
// arity -- `add(E)` and `add(int, E)`, `put(K, V)`, `set(int, E)` -- and a generator matches
